# Docs metadata: README tables, SECURITY table and the "At a glance" box are generated from
# this (dev/gen-docs.py). One "key: value" per line.
emoji: 🔐
name: Signal hardening
group: extras
what: Signal's database key in the wallet instead of plain text; it asks for the wallet password first and quits after 15 minutes idle (both adjustable in Wallet apps).
why: A headset gets passed around: shared with family, often without a SteamOS login password. Flathub Signal otherwise keeps its key in plain text.
changes: Signal's menu entry (Wallet apps: password first, Close-after timer), a Flatpak override for Signal, Signal's `config.json`
access: Asks for the wallet password first; quits Signal when idle; key in the wallet
survives-updates: Yes (everything is in your home folder)
undo: `./install.sh uninstall signal` (Signal keeps using the wallet: switching back would lock you out of its data)
